          up: {"title":"Tap every turnaround document (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>A longer extract from the Roseau Water Sports Club office log. Several lines are designed to look like turnaround documents but are not.</p>","q":"Tap EVERY line that describes a turnaround document.","lines":["A member's handwritten letter asking to change her contact details.","A renewal notice printed with the member's details, returned with her signature and payment.","The barcode on a rental kayak, scanned at check-out.","An event booking slip printed at the bottom of the club newsletter, filled in and handed back by members.","A survey printed by the club and returned by members with their answers.","A new member's application form, filled in by hand.","A cheque written by a member and handed in with no club form.","The tear-off stub of the mooring-fee bill, returned with payment.","A printed receipt the club gives a member after payment, which the member keeps."],"correct":[1,3,4,7],"win":"Excellent. The renewal notice, newsletter booking slip, survey and mooring-fee stub were all produced by the club, sent out and returned as input. The letter, application form and cheque were never produced by the club's system, and the receipt is never returned.","miss":"A turnaround document must pass BOTH tests: the club's system produced it, AND it comes back as input. Check each line against both tests."}
