          up: {"title":"Which type is it? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","q":"An electricity company prints each bill with a barcode on the tear-off stub, which customers return with payment. Which statement BEST classifies the stub?","options":[{"t":"It is only a source document, because the payment data is recorded on it.","fb":"The account data was already in the system; the system produced the stub, so it is not where the data is first recorded."},{"t":"It is neither, because it is printed on paper.","fb":"Being on paper does not decide the category. Its role in processing does."},{"t":"It is only machine-readable, because it has a barcode.","fb":"The barcode makes it machine-readable, but this ignores that it is sent out and returned, which makes it turnaround too."},{"t":"It is a turnaround document, because the system produced it and it returns as input, AND it is machine-readable, because its barcode is scanned directly.","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. The stub fits two categories, and this answer gives the feature that proves each one."}]}
